     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>I am having trouble understanding how two very similar reads give different results when using featureCounts with --read2pos.<br><br>Here are the two reads:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">$ zcat </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.fastq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gz<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">@HWI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">700819F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">303</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C6WYKACXX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2113</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9364</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">95721</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">UMI_AAAAGGGG </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">AGGGAAGC<br>GCTGTTCTACAGCTATGGCCGGGCCAGCTGCAGCTTTCCGCCGCTTGGGCGCCTTGTCCGGAGCTGCGGCCTTAGGCTTCGCTTCCTACGGG<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>FFFFFIIIIIFIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIFFFFFFFFFFFBFFFBFBBBBBFFFBFFFFFBFFFFFBFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFB<br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">@HWI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">700819F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">303</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C6WYKACXX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2314</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4761</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">64177</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">UMI_AAAAGGGG </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">AGGGAAGC<br>GCTGTTCTACAGCTATGGCCGGGCCAGCTGCAGCTTTCCGCCGCTTGGGCGCCTTGTCCGGAGCTGCGGCCTTAGGCTTCGCTTC<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>FFBF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7BFFFFFIIFBFFFFFFF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">B0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BBBFBBFFBBBBBB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">07BBB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BBB7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">00</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">B7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7BB</span></div></code></div><br>They start the same, but are different lengths because they were quality trimmed from the 3&#39; end. When I search with BLAT, they are similar as expected. They both map to the reverse strand, have the same end position (their 5&#39; end), and the match starts at the second base of the query sequence (the first G does not map to the genome).<br><br><tt><pre>   ACTIONS      QUERY           SCORE START  END QSIZE IDENTITY CHRO STRAND  START    END      SPAN\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n<a href=\"http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position=chr17:7307326-7307416&amp;db=hg19&amp;ss=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_4293_ddab90.pslx+../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_4293_ddab90.fa&amp;hgsid=485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position%3Dchr17:7307326-7307416%26db%3Dhg19%26ss%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_4293_ddab90.pslx%2B../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_4293_ddab90.fa%26hgsid%3D485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3N6nfPkHHTnBlWK-v_RwN4\">browser</a> <a href=\"http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgc?o=7307325&amp;g=htcUserAli&amp;i=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_4293_ddab90.pslx+..%2Ftrash%2FhgSs%2FhgSs_www_4293_ddab90.fa+YourSeq&amp;c=chr17&amp;l=7307325&amp;r=7307416&amp;db=hg19&amp;hgsid=485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgc?o%3D7307325%26g%3DhtcUserAli%26i%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_4293_ddab90.pslx%2B..%252Ftrash%252FhgSs%252FhgSs_www_4293_ddab90.fa%2BYourSeq%26c%3Dchr17%26l%3D7307325%26r%3D7307416%26db%3Dhg19%26hgsid%3D485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07qDmd7y5QAxA7edpOdT_2\">details</a> YourSeq           91     2    92    92 100.0%    17   -    7307326   7307416     91</pre></tt><br><tt><pre>  ACTIONS      QUERY           SCORE START  END QSIZE IDENTITY CHRO STRAND  START    END      SPAN\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n<a href=\"http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position=chr17:7307333-7307416&amp;db=hg19&amp;ss=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_454f_ddb450.pslx+../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_454f_ddb450.fa&amp;hgsid=485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position%3Dchr17:7307333-7307416%26db%3Dhg19%26ss%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_454f_ddb450.pslx%2B../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_454f_ddb450.fa%26hgsid%3D485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw28FdgcpW57BcxpayLXwiZV\">browser</a> <a href=\"http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgc?o=7307332&amp;g=htcUserAli&amp;i=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_454f_ddb450.pslx+..%2Ftrash%2FhgSs%2FhgSs_www_454f_ddb450.fa+YourSeq&amp;c=chr17&amp;l=7307332&amp;r=7307416&amp;db=hg19&amp;hgsid=485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgc?o%3D7307332%26g%3DhtcUserAli%26i%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_454f_ddb450.pslx%2B..%252Ftrash%252FhgSs%252FhgSs_www_454f_ddb450.fa%2BYourSeq%26c%3Dchr17%26l%3D7307332%26r%3D7307416%26db%3Dhg19%26hgsid%3D485870845_CKaQawArt2WNyAkEyBsAQugE1HFq&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08sAYvlQEQh8VSQm2RcPfU\">details</a> YourSeq           84     2    85    85 100.0%    17   -    7307333   7307416     84</pre></tt><br>I map these to sequences to human genome hg19 with subjunc:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">$ subjunc </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i genome</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">combined </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">r </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.fastq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gz </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">u </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.bam</span></div></code></div><br>Already at this step the two sequences start to diverge. Both have one non-matching base, but only the first read has the soft-clipped base in its CIGAR.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">$ samtools view </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.bam</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>HWI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">700819F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">303</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C6WYKACXX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2113</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9364</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">95721</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">UMI_AAAAGGGG    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">16</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    chr17    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7307326</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">59</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">91M1S</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    CCCGTAGGAAGCGAAGCCTAAGGCCGCAGCTCCGGACAAGGCGCCCAAGCGGCGGAAAGCTGCAGCTGGCCCGGCCATAGCTGTAGAACAGC    BFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFBFFFFFBFFFFFBFFFBBBBBFBFFFBFFFFFFFFFFFIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIFIIIIIFFFFF    HI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    NH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    NM</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>HWI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">700819F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">303</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C6WYKACXX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2314</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4761</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">64177</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">UMI_AAAAGGGG    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">16</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    chr17    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7307333</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">58</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">85M</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    GAAGCGAAGCCTAAGGCCGCAGCTCCGGACAAGGCGCCCAAGCGGCGGAAAGCTGCAGCTGGCCCGGCCATAGCTGTAGAACAGC    BB7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">00</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7BBB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BBB70</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BBBBBBFFBBFBBB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">BB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FFFFFFFBFIIFFFFFB7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FBFF    HI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    NH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    NM</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><br>Next I use featureCounts to get gene counts.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">$ featureCounts </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.saf</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F SAF </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">--</span><span style=\"color:#000\">read2pos </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">o </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.txt</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.bam</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I use strand-specific counting and reduce the read to the most 5&#39; base. Because of the BLAT results that the 5 &#39; ends of both sequences map to chr17:7,307,416, I&#39;d expect featureCounts to give the same assignment for both sequences. However, this is not the case. The first is determined to be ambiguous due to multi-mapping to 3 separate genes, but the second is assigned to just one of the three.<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">$ cat </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2016</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">03</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">31.bam</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">featureCounts <br>HWI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">700819F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">303</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C6WYKACXX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2113</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9364</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">95721</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">UMI_AAAAGGGG    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Unassigned_Ambiguity</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Number_Of_Overlapped_Genes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>HWI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">700819F</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">303</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C6WYKACXX</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2314</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4761</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">64177</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">UMI_AAAAGGGG    </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Assigned</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    ENSG00000205544    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>How is this possible? Is the soft-clipped base in the CIGAR of the one read changing the position featureCounts uses for read2pos? Is the correct end of the read being used? Since it is mapped to the reverse strand, the end position should be used. If I change `--read2pos` to 3 or do not use it, both reads are classified as ambiguous.<br><br>I am using the binary subread-1.5.0-p1-Linux-x86_64. All these files are available to download from Dropbox:<br><br><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ne6jwd0gsyfxgzj/2016-03-31.fastq.gz?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/ne6jwd0gsyfxgzj/2016-03-31.fastq.gz?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13sgYjquktW8m5wsculNxm\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/ne6jwd0gsyfxgzj/2016-03-31.fastq.gz?dl=0</a><br><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/dzawbx878dv0pyc/2016-03-31.bam?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/dzawbx878dv0pyc/2016-03-31.bam?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YKOKWthgSIgI0brAynZrn\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/dzawbx878dv0pyc/2016-03-31.bam?dl=0</a><br><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/dkhzfq2ogvrnkeq/2016-03-31.txt?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/dkhzfq2ogvrnkeq/2016-03-31.txt?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234525630000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-38w52M1UDPpiHv8sIF-M\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/dkhzfq2ogvrnkeq/2016-03-31.txt?dl=0</a><br><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/0b3fojp6hrc6xe